While this probably shouldn't apply to altars, does anyone else think
it would be interesting to have a player-to-player trade/gift system on
NAO? I've been considering writing a patch to do that, but I'd like to
know if there's any interest in the idea first. I would probably choose
to do gifts by having the mail daemon deliver a package ("box of
holding" to stop players becoming encumbered at inconvenient moments?)
which contains the object and optionally a message. Trading would be a
bit harder... to guard against cheating, we need the mail daemon to act
as an arbitrater:
 * Alice makes a trade offer to Bob, giving her trade goods to the
daemon.
 * The daemon tells Bob of the offer and any covering message from
Alice. Bob may decline the offer (optionally with a message), in which
case the daemon returns Alice's goods.
 * Otherwise, Bob makes a counter-offer and gives his goods to the
daemon.
 * The daemon tells Alice of Bob's counter-offer and message. Alice can
decline (in which case everyone's goods are returned); again,
optionally with a message.
 * Otherwise, the deal is set and the daemon passes both sets of goods
to their new owners.

Obviously unique objects cannot be sent to other players. Artifacts
will resist the attempt, unique corpses turn into slime molds or
somesuch?


